.TH LUS-HELP 1 "" "Lus" "Lus Manual"
.SH NAME
lus-help \- print the standard library reference for a name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBlus help\fR [name | module | \-\-search text]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the reference of the standard library in the terminal.
The reference is part of the executable, so it describes the version that is running.
With a name such as \fBstring.find\fR or \fBtcp_socket:receive\fR, it prints the signature, the permissions the call needs, the stability, and the description.
With a module such as \fBfs.path\fR, it lists the entries of the module.
With no argument, it lists the modules.
When the name matches no entry, it lists the names that contain it and exits with status 1.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-search text\fR, \fB\-s text\fR
List the entries whose name or description contains \fBtext\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
The reference was printed.
.TP
1
No entry has the name.
.TP
2
An option is malformed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lus (1)
.PP
The CLI page of the Lus manual, https://lus.dev/manual/cli#lus-help, has the same text with links to the rest of the manual.
